        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.
        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.

        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by the failure to properly initialize the Helix cluster and add instances when the cluster was not yet fully set up, leading to AMS stopping unexpectedly after a Resource Update. The original implementation lacked error handling and retries, causing it to miss instances that needed to be added to the cluster.

        Commit message:
        AMBARI-21593 : AMS stopped after RU [AMS distributed mode
 with 2 collectors] (avijayan)  

        Patch:
